@page "/docs/components/badge"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Badge
<PageTitle>Badge - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Badge</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="badge" />
        </div>
        <p>Ten variants, from solid and status colors to outline, ghost and link. A badge can carry an icon or a count, and <code>RenderAs</code> turns it into a link or any other element without losing the styling.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(BadgeUsageExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Variants" Example="typeof(BadgeVariantsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With icon" Example="typeof(BadgeIconExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Counts" Description="A badge holds a number as easily as text. For a round counter, add `size-5 rounded-full p-0` through `Class`." Example="typeof(BadgeCountsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="As a link" Description="Use `RenderAs` to put the badge styling on an anchor, so it navigates like any other link." Example="typeof(BadgeRenderAsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Classes passed through `Class` are merged over the variant defaults, which covers brand colors, status tints and gradients."
          Example="typeof(BadgeCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, a leading icon sits to the right of the label."
          Example="typeof(BadgeRtlExample)" />
</div>

